{
  "quest.3E8FE865C4FAA360.quest_desc": [
    "A sprig holding mutative magic. It is the tool that builds most of the mod's living contraptions.",
    "",
    "&aGrasspers&r, &2Critter Snares&r, Wormwood, Parasitic Lice and Owls all start here, and it converts a handful of blocks into other blocks besides.",
  ],
  "quest.511C982980D29F6B.title": "&bAncient Tablets",
  "quest.2AAC5AE4E1520348.quest_desc": [
    "A &dNecromantic Stone&r is an &aAttuned Stone&r remade by a night-time rite. Nearly everything in &eForbidden Magic&r starts with one.",
    "",
    "The rite only runs at night. Draw a small ring of &aRitual Chalk&r around &6Golden Ritual Chalk&r and keep 1,000 &bAltar Power&r in range. The book lists the reagents.",
    "",
    "Make several. The &aBrazier&r below needs one, and so do the soulbind, the &bBind Phylactery&r rite and the &bRite of Severed Soul&r.",
  ],
  "quest.4BBF3655536142E9.quest_desc": [
    "A &bTaglock&r captures the essence of a creature or player and turns it into a link you can point magic at. Most of the binding half of this mod runs through them.",
    "",
    "This quest path opens as soon as you have the book. You can also lift a taglock from a bed somebody slept in recently.",
    "",
    "Mobs are easy, but players are not. A taglock taken from a player expires after seven days, and taking one in plain sight or bright light usually fails. Come at them from behind, sneaking, or while invisible.",
    "",
    "&7&oA taglock of yourself is worth keeping. Several protective items want one.&r",
  ],
  "quest.354E14D2455E5317.title": "The Spinning Wheel",
  "quest.39F2353FFE78EA20.quest_desc": [
    "The &dAltar&r generates &bAltar Power&r, which nearly everything else in the mod runs on. Build it near your workshop and everything in range draws from it.",
    "",
    "One of its ingredients is a pair of &aRowan Logs&r, and Rowan only exists because &dMutandis&r made it. Mutate a sapling until it turns into a Rowan Sapling and grow that out first.",
    "",
    "The &dDeepslate Altar Blocks&r are where your first two oven fumes go. Place six of them in a 3x1x2 arrangement and the multiblock forms itself.",
    "",
    "Power scales with the nature around it. Trees, flowers and grass all count, so an altar in a stone room is a weak altar.",
    "",
    "It takes up to six modifiers on top:",
    "- &bHeads&r: a multiplier and a flat boost.",
    "- &bLights&r: a multiplier.",
    "- &aChalice&r: a flat boost.",
    "- &bRange modifiers&r: push the power further out.",
    "- &dPentacle&r: doubles power outright.",
  ],
  "quest.7B33A66F4C09D967.quest_desc": [
    "A &aFume Extension&r goes beside the &2Oven&r. Each one adds 20% to the fume chance and speeds up cooking, so two of them raise a cook from 25% to 65%.",
    "",
    "You can fit two, one on the left and one on the right of the oven's front.",
  ],
  "quest.4DC258DC240CB01A.quest_desc": [
    "&bCoven Witches&r are the witches who join your coven. Each one you recruit with a signed &aCoven Contract&r counts toward the bigger rites.",
    "",
    "A coven rite counts the coven witches within 16 blocks of the &6Golden Ritual Chalk&r. If you carry a &aSeer Stone&r, any recruited witches who are missing are called to the circle.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    " Coven huts are rare, so the &bSummon Coven Witch&r rite makes one instead. It needs an ordinary witch as a sacrifice, and &bSummon Witch&r ritual can easily bring a witch to you.",
    "",
    "&cUse a blank contract.&r The rite eats the one you put in, and losing the signed one disbands your coven.",
  ],
  "quest.5BE987F72F75E6B4.quest_desc": [
    "Custom potions start with &aNether Wart&r in a lit &2Cauldron&r with an &dAltar&r in range, then you add ingredients one at a time.",
    "",
    "&bCapacity&r limits how much you can stack into one brew, and stronger ingredients drain more &bAltar Power&r. JEI's Cauldron Brewing recipes show each ingredient's Altar Power cost, and a finished brew's tooltip lists the Capacity each ingredient used.",
    "",
    "Decide the whole order before you start. There is no undo once a brew is part-built, only &aWood Ash&r and starting over.",
  ],
  "quest.75833FE4473ACD2F.title": "&dThe Cauldron",
  "quest.44AFF4B7385115C5.title": "&6The Lich Eternal",
  "task.23053105A5CEA741.title": "Read an Ancient Tablet",
  "quest.22D3C16250EAAB17.quest_desc": [
    "Drinking this splits you from your body. The body stays where you stood as a shell holding your whole inventory, and you float free as a spirit.",
    "",
    "A &5Lich&r with &bSoul Form&r can step into undead mobs, illagers and zombie villagers from there. Anyone else gets back in with the &bRite of Soulbind&r, which only works on a waxing or full moon, so set it up before you drink.",
    "",
    "The &bRite of Severed Soul&r works through a taglock instead. Aimed at a villager, it kills the villager and leaves an ethereal copy that a &dSoul Cage&r will take.",
    "",
    "&cThe shell dies after a few hits.&r Hide it before you leave.",
  ],
  "quest.59F9E4D81168E7B6.title": "The Other Chalks",
  "quest.3A6004A6F9AA8A10.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a &aBrazier&r with any glass block and it becomes a &dSoul Cage&r. Breaking the cage gives you the brazier back.",
    "",
    "A cage pulls in the nearest raised villager or zombie villager within 8 blocks and keeps its soul. Kill a villager, raise the corpse with the &aWitches Hand&r and let the cage take it.",
    "",
    "Your first bound soul is level 2, but only if you stand within 8 blocks of the cage while it binds. Each cage holds one soul, so build a row of them.",
    "",
    "Level 2 gives you &bSummon Undead&r, which raises the corpses around you without using infusion charge.",
  ],
  "quest.39F2353FFE78EA20.title": "&dThe Altar",
  "task.329249CAA612F688.title": "Any Cauldron, iron or copper",
  "quest.59429D6ED1EBF212.title": "The Binding of Souls",
  "quest.2AAC5AE4E1520348.title": "Necromantic Stone",
  "quest.34FC6EDF6C1D4200.quest_desc": [
    "The second tablet covers levels 6 to 8, and none of it counts until you have read that tablet.",
    "",
    "- &bLevel 6&r: use &bLife Drain&r on five animals.",
    "- &bLevel 7&r: leave your body with &bSoul Form&r, move into a zombie villager, an undead mob or an illager, and kill a villager while you are possessing it.",
    "- &bLevel 8&r: kill the &cWither&r.",
    "",
    "Soul Form leaves your body behind as a shell that holds your whole inventory. &cIt dies after a few hits&r, so leave it somewhere safe.",
  ],
  "quest.43D715B893372DC6.title": "The Witches Hand",
  "quest.0D1C211E62DB361A.quest_desc": [
    "Binds two creatures together and pushes most of what happens to the first one onto the second.",
    "",
    "It can be carried or placed in the world, so it does not tie up an inventory slot the way the death poppet does.",
  ],
  "quest.52B5ABFD7DA5E75A.title": "Soulstone Pendant",
  "quest.75833FE4473ACD2F.quest_desc": [
    "Every witch's workshop is built around this. Brews, potions and most of the mod's crafting happen in here.",
    "",
    "Fill it with water and light it with &aFlint and Steel&r before you use it. Stronger recipes want an &dAltar&r in range as well, which comes a couple of quests from now.",
    "",
    "A pinch of &aWood Ash&r empties it when a brew goes wrong.",
  ],
  "quest.3BC3912753C84805.title": "Cauldron Infusion",
  "quest.129860E2C9082F1C.title": "&cThe Voodoo Poppet",
  "quest.4DC258DC240CB01A.title": "The Coven",
  "quest.659C0BF1D4150E50.quest_desc": [
    "One of the four long paths, and one of the two that change how you eat.",
    "",
    "A vampire runs on a blood pool instead of hunger. The &aBlood Crucible&r is where you store it, filled from a &2Bottle of Blood&r or a Wine Glass, and your vampire children will carry their night's harvest back to it.",
    "",
    "&aBloodstone Pendant&r in a curio slot stretches how long you can hold bat form. Sunlight is the obvious problem and the book explains the rest.",
    "",
    "&7&oThis is a whole progression with its own bloodlines. Treat the vampirism section of the book as the real quest line.&r",
  ],
  "quest.2A53B680B919D776.title": "&dMutandis",
  "quest.69A98E479FA0D905.quest_desc": [
    "A pocket heart transplant. It spends itself to save its owner from one death, then it is gone.",
    "",
    "This one cannot be placed in the world. It has to be carried.",
    "",
    "The same family covers the smaller problems: &aArmor Protection&r fully repairs your armor right before it breaks, and &2Hunger Protection&r tops up your food bar now and then.",
    "",
    "Its &aDrop of Luck&r needs parts from the &2Distillery&r. It also needs &aMutandis Extremis&r, so this quest waits on both.",
  ],
  "quest.25B6E92B02340718.quest_desc": [
    "Imps from the &bSummon Imp&r rite trade in souls. Right-click one and it offers reagents and a contract, paid for with the souls around you.",
    "",
    "It counts every ethereal creature and every filled &dSoul Cage&r within 16 blocks of you. A caged villager is worth 200 and the contract costs 500.",
    "",
    "The &dPetrification Contract&r teaches the &bPetrify&r glyph, which turns one creature to stone for a short time. The &bRite of Petrification&r does the same to everything around the circle, you included.",
  ],
  "quest.354E14D2455E5317.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSpinning Wheel&r spins magical threads and fabrics out of the odder things you have collected.",
    "",
    "Most of its recipes pull &bAltar Power&r, so keep it in range of the &dAltar&r like everything else.",
  ],
  "task.6E08A194E248D650.title": "Any Fume Extension, iron or copper",
  "quest.54C808CC43A93EC0.title": "The Distillery",
  "quest.59F9E4D81168E7B6.quest_desc": [
    "Bigger rites need better chalk. Each one draws a different ring of the same circle.",
    "",
    "- &6Golden Ritual Chalk&r: the standard second ring.",
    "- &cInfernal Chalk&r: for the rites that deal with demons.",
    "- &dOtherwhere Chalk&r: for anything reaching into another world.",
    "- &aBinding Chalk&r: for the rites that tie something down.",
  ],
  "quest.720DB36A13C6BBDC.quest_desc": [
    "Witchcraft here is a workshop craft. You grow strange plants, boil them down in a &aCauldron&r, and bind the results to people and places.",
    "",
    "It starts in the grass. Whenever short or tall grass drops &2Wheat Seeds&r, it has a one in twenty chance to drop each Witchery seed as well. That makes &aBelladonna&r and &2Mandrake&r turn up roughly once per 160 grass blocks each. &aSnowbell&r and &2Water Artichoke&r drop just as often. So does &aWolfsbane&r.",
    "",
    "The &dHedge Witch&r sells all five for 20 coins each, and her shop opens as soon as you carry one. She keeps shop in witch huts, swamp houses, mangrove huts and dark forest settlements.",
    "",
    "Plant the &aBelladonna&r first. Its flower is the one ingredient the &dGuidebook&r needs, and nothing else in the mod opens until you have a garden going.",
    "",
    "&aMandrake&r wakes up in daylight. Pull a ripe one while it is awake and it jumps out of the ground and runs, so you have to chase it down for the root. At night it is often asleep and gives up the root straight away.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Rites, brews, symbology spells and afflictions also level your \", {\"text\": \"Magic skill tree\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ftb:skills,ftb:magic.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Skill Trees guide\"}}, \".\"]",
  ],
  "quest.0E9C90976C66641C.quest_desc": [
    "A plant that catches small mobs. Slimes, bats and silverfish walk in and stay there.",
    "",
    "It needs four &aAlder Saplings&r, water, a cobweb and a zombie to grow. What you catch matters later. A snare holding a bat is a step toward an &dOwl&r familiar, and one holding a silverfish leads to the &aParasitic Louse&r.",
  ],
  "quest.54C808CC43A93EC0.quest_desc": [
    "The &aDistillery&r splits fumes and reagents into purer parts. Most of its recipes also use up empty &2Jars&r, so keep a stack beside it.",
    "",
    "&aGypsum&r and &2Tear of the Goddess&r for &dRitual Chalk&r both come out of here.",
    "",
    "Both this and the &aSpinning Wheel&r need an &2Attuned Stone&r to build, and both draw &bAltar Power&r while they work. Cook a few rowan saplings for &aWhiff of Magic&r before you start, since the stone is made from it.",
  ],
  "quest.4D2974A8DC0256BA.quest_desc": [
    "Use an &2Arthana&r to kill undead. This will drop &dSpectral Dust&r used for most rituals.",
  ],
  "quest.77FAC5980E0A7A5D.quest_desc": [
    "Sign the &aContract&r and you can gather a coven of players and witches.",
    "",
    "A witch may want a favour before she joins, and the more powerful your coven already is, the more the next one will ask for.",
    "",
    "&cGuard the contract.&r Destroying it disbands the whole coven.",
  ],
  "quest.58BC157CB468BAD7.title": "&dRitual Chalk",
  "quest.2A53B680B919D776.quest_desc": [
    "&dMutandis&r mutates plants into other plants. Use it on something growing and it becomes something else.",
    "",
    "Brewing it takes an &aExhale of the Horned One&r in the &dCauldron&r, so the &aOven&r has to be running first for that fume.",
    "",
    "JEI lists 500 &bAltar Power&r for it, but the cauldron makes it with no &dAltar&r nearby.",
    "",
    "The useful part is the cooldown. For a short while after each use it will only affect that same plant type, so you can keep applying it to walk through the possible results instead of starting over each time.",
    "",
    "That is how you get the Rowan, Alder and Hawthorn saplings the rest of the mod needs. None of those trees grow wild.",
  ],
  "quest.5B9A6795C7A9747A.title": "Infernal Chalk is Fire!",
  "quest.59429D6ED1EBF212.quest_desc": [
    "The first tablet covers levels 3 to 5. Progress only counts while you are at the level it belongs to, so work through them in order.",
    "",
    "- &bLevel 3&r: one of your raised zombies has to kill a mob.",
    "- &bLevel 4&r: kill five golems yourself. Snow golems count, and kills by your servants do not.",
    "- &bLevel 5&r: bind two more villager souls, for three in total.",
    "",
    "Each level adds an ability. &bCorpse Explosion&r blows up your own raised dead without breaking blocks, &bLife Drain&r damages one target for up to five seconds, and &bDeath Teleport&r comes at level 5.",
    "",
    "&cLevel 3 costs you a heart of maximum health.",
  ],
  "task.596AE248E0C0BB3C.title": "Bind a soul in a Soul Cage",
  "quest.34FC6EDF6C1D4200.title": "The Severed Soul",
  "quest.720DB36A13C6BBDC.title": "All Begins With The Green",
  "quest.07C62222A3914CD9.quest_desc": [
    "The third path leaves your body behind. Drink &dBrew of Sleeping&r in the Overworld and you wake up somewhere else.",
    "",
    "Where you land is not fixed. It can be the calm &bDream&r or the hostile &cNightmare&r, and &aWispy Cotton&r, &2Flowing Spirit&r and Dream Weavers of Nightmares near your body all push the odds toward the good one.",
    "",
    "&cApple of Sleeping&r skips the coin flip and sends you straight to the Nightmare.",
  ],
  "quest.29656D8C06B7A2F7.title": "&cLycanthropy",
  "quest.0D1C211E62DB361A.title": "&cThe Vampiric Poppet",
  "quest.24ACDC2BB0A27070.title": "The Phylactery's Embrace",
  "quest.1289B963EA711CAD.title": "The Waystone",
  "quest.7F82D5208B9CB9C9.quest_desc": [
    "A &dDemon&r can be summoned by using an &cInfernal Ritual&r. The &dDemon Blood&r is going to be needed for brews and rituals.",
    "",
    "You can use the &bBinding Ritual&r to keep the demon from escaping. You do not want him getting away. Kill him and take its heart to refine into &dDemon Blood&r.",
  ],
  "quest.0D831CA92D518208.quest_desc": [
    "The stronger form. It does everything ordinary &dMutandis&r does and then reaches past plants.",
    "",
    "It works on wheat, cactus and sugar cane, turns grass into mycelium, and converts dirt under water into clay.",
  ],
  "quest.4BBF3655536142E9.title": "&bTaglocks",
  "quest.44B05983766D847B.quest_desc": [
    "A &dPoppet&r is an empty doll. Craft one together with a &bTaglock&r and it binds to whoever that taglock came from.",
    "",
    "Read each poppet's requirement before you rely on it. Some have to stay in the owner's inventory to work, and the ones that do not can be placed in the world instead, which keeps them out of reach.",
    "",
    "The doll needs &aSpanish Moss&r, which comes from using &dMutandis&r on vines. &dThe Hedge Witch&r also sells blank poppets.",
  ],
  "task.57B5F9A76FCB6A34.title": "Read a second Ancient Tablet",
  "quest.58BC157CB468BAD7.quest_desc": [
    "Rituals are drawn, not crafted. &dRitual Chalk&r marks a circle on the ground, you place the reagents, and the rite runs.",
    "",
    "Chalk marks are consumed by the ritual, so keep making more. The &dGuidebook&r ritual section is the catalog and it is the largest section in the book.",
  ],
  "quest.4E0BA295792F02DF.title": "Wormwood",
  "quest.22D3C16250EAAB17.title": "Brew of Soul Severance",
  "quest.2CF31599FE4D718C.quest_desc": [
    "This plant holds an item for you. Rituals read what a &aGrassper&r is holding, which is how you feed a circle its reagents without standing there dropping things.",
    "",
    "Grow one from four grass, a chest and water using the &aMutating Sprig&r.",
  ],
  "quest.47F71E08732A4852.quest_desc": [
    "The &aOven&r burns saplings down to &2Wood Ash&r. Each cook has a 25% chance of leaving a fume behind. Fumes escape unless there is somewhere to catch them, so keep fired &aJars&r in the jar slot. Clay jars sit in that slot and catch nothing, so smelt them first.",
    "",
    "The sapling decides which fume you get. Birch gives &aBreath of the Goddess&r and oak gives &aExhale of the Horned One&r, which are the two the &dAltar&r wants next. Rowan gives &aWhiff of Magic&r for later. The book lists the rest.",
    "",
    "Copper ovens exist and oxidize like any other copper, but they behave the same.",
  ],
  "quest.511C982980D29F6B.quest_desc": [
    "&bAncient Tablets&r are carved into the &bAncient Cities&r of the Deep Dark, and only a necromancer can read one. Stand within 10 blocks while infused and look at it for seven seconds, until it glows.",
    "",
    "The first tablet makes you a &5Lich&r. From then on the mod shows your next requirement on screen.",
    "",
    "There are three to read and each one counts once. Read every one you find on the trip. Progress toward level 6 waits for the second tablet, and progress toward level 9 waits for the third.",
    "",
    "&cA Lich stops getting hungry.&r The hunger bar stays at six drumsticks with no saturation, so food never heals you again. Keep healing potions close.",
  ],
  "quest.77FAC5980E0A7A5D.title": "The Coven Contract",
  "quest.2CF31599FE4D718C.title": "The Grassper",
  "quest.5B9A6795C7A9747A.quest_desc": [
    "Having &dInfernal Chalk&r opens many rituals.",
    "",
    "- You can summon a &cDemon&r to bind and trade with.",
    "- You can Summon a &aSpectral Pig&r which is another way to get &bSpectral Dust&r.",
    "",
    "Many other rituals open with this chalk and the rites are quite dangerous. ",
  ],
  "quest.7F82D5208B9CB9C9.title": "Summon a Demon",
  "quest.62B1F0F9D5F9895A.quest_desc": [
    "A bramble that hurts to touch and throws whatever touched it a long way away. Useful as a wall, unpleasant to walk into.",
    "",
    "Put &aSpanish Moss&r on all four sides of a sugar cane, each piece over still water. Set four &2Grasspers&r on the corners holding four Ender Pearls between them, then use the Mutating Sprig on the cane.",
    "",
    "&aWild Bramble&r is the cheaper cousin. Break that one with a golden tool or it spreads.",
  ],
  "quest.36038380E0C3F405.title": "&5Lichdom",
  "quest.36038380E0C3F405.quest_desc": [
    "The fourth long path. A &5Lich&r raises the dead to fight for it and can come back from dying, and it gives up most of its natural healing for that.",
    "",
    "Brew the &dNecromantic Soulbind&r first. It costs a &aTotem of Undying&r, so get two, because you need the second one for the rite.",
    "",
    "The &bInfuse Necromancy&r rite wants 4,000 &bAltar Power&r, &6Golden Ritual Chalk&r in the center and two rings of ordinary chalk. It consumes the soulbind and then hits you for 100 magic damage.",
    "",
    "&cYou have to survive it.&r Hold a &aTotem of Undying&r or carry a &6Death Protection Poppet&r. If you die, the infusion does not take and the soulbind is gone.",
  ],
  "quest.0C9BBC137D055B80.title": "Lifeblood",
  "quest.4D2974A8DC0256BA.title": "More than just a ritual blade",
  "quest.43D715B893372DC6.quest_desc": [
    "Your infusion only works while you hold a &aWitches Hand&r. Witches drop one about half the time, and the &bSummon Witch&r rite brings a witch to you.",
    "",
    "Hold it and the corpses of undead mobs, villagers and pillagers that died nearby show up as soul particles. Hold right-click and let go to spend 500 infusion charge and raise every corpse within 8 blocks of where you are looking.",
    "",
    "The raised dead fight for you, but only for a minute at first. They last longer as you level and stay for good at level 10. The &bRite of Charging&r refills your charge.",
  ],
  "quest.74CB218EFCB2185A.title": "&dJust Another Witchery Remake",
  "quest.4E0BA295792F02DF.quest_desc": [
    "Use a &dBrew of Sleeping&r to visit the &bDream World&r. &aWispy Cotton&r can be found in the &bDream World&r it cannot be found in the &cNightmare World&r. ",
    "",
    "&aWormwood&r is the necromancy plant. The &aBrazier&r and most of the death-flavored rituals want it.",
    "",
    "Grow it from wheat with four &aWispy Cotton&r and four water using the &2Mutating Sprig&r.",
  ],
  "quest.21812817F84A52D1.title": "The Brazier",
  "quest.3A6004A6F9AA8A10.title": "&dThe Soul Cage",
  "quest.25B6E92B02340718.title": "The Petrification Contract",
  "quest.3BC3912753C84805.quest_desc": [
    "Several of the named brews can put an enchantment straight onto your gear. JEI's Cauldron Infusion recipes show which brew gives which enchantment and what it goes on.",
    "",
    "Finish one of those brews in a lit &2Cauldron&r with an &dAltar&r in range and leave it there, then throw in the item you want enchanted. It comes back out enchanted and the cauldron empties, so one brew enchants one item.",
    "",
    "A bottled brew can't be poured back in, but bottling part of it is fine as long as some is left. Each infusion takes 2,500 &bAltar Power&r, or 5,000 for a &2Hags Ring&r.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: An item that doesn't match a recipe, already has that enchantment at that level or higher, or goes in while the &dAltar&r is short of power is taken in as a brewing ingredient instead.",
  ],
  "quest.0C9BBC137D055B80.quest_desc": [
    "&dLifeblood&r is a vine grown from a living soul. Eating a berry heals a heart and, if you have none, gives you a &dLifeblood&r heart that takes damage before your own health and refills over time.",
    "",
    "Place a cobweb with a villager standing in it, or with a filled &dSoul Cage&r right next to it. Put cave vines on the four diagonal corners one block below the web and chorus on the four corners one block above, then use a &aMutating Sprig&r on the web.",
    "",
    "The villager or the caged soul is used up. Pick the berries by hand and break the vines with shears to move them.",
  ],
  "quest.3E8FE865C4FAA360.title": "The Mutating Sprig",
  "quest.7B33A66F4C09D967.title": "More Fumes",
  "quest.1289B963EA711CAD.quest_desc": [
    "Use a &aWaystone&r on a block to record that spot. The stone now points at it.",
    "",
    "Teleportation and the rituals that reach across distance all read a bound waystone rather than coordinates you type in.",
  ],
  "quest.62B1F0F9D5F9895A.title": "&cEnder Bramble",
  "task.21C294004DC52F4E.title": "Reach Lich level 5",
  "quest.659C0BF1D4150E50.title": "&cVampirism",
  "quest.21812817F84A52D1.quest_desc": [
    "The &aBrazier&r burns ingredients as incense and spreads the result to everything nearby. Light it with &aFlint and Steel&r or a fire charge.",
    "",
    "Building one takes a &dNecromantic Stone&r, which is why it comes after that rite.",
    "",
    "The &aCenser&r is the potion version. Right-click it with any potion and every creature within sixteen blocks gets that effect for as long as the potion lasts.",
    "",
    "Most of the brazier incenses want &aWormwood&r, and the stronger ones want a few hundred &bAltar Power&r before they will start.",
  ],
  "quest.69A98E479FA0D905.title": "&6Death Protection Poppet",
  "quest.52B5ABFD7DA5E75A.quest_desc": [
    "A necklace that gives a &5Lich&r one more soul slot, so one more phylactery can hold a soul for you.",
    "",
    "It goes in the necklace curio slot. &cTaking it off empties a phylactery&r to get you back under the limit.",
    "",
    "&7&oYour own slots grow as you level. One to start, two from level 4 and three from level 6&r",
  ],
  "quest.5BE987F72F75E6B4.title": "&bBrews and Custom Potions",
  "task.2CCA016A76895907.title": "Read a third Ancient Tablet",
  "quest.47F71E08732A4852.title": "The Witches Oven",
  "quest.44AFF4B7385115C5.quest_desc": [
    "Level 10 wants three phylactery saves within ten minutes. You need three filled phylacteries and three deaths close together, so plan the deaths as carefully as the souls.",
    "",
    "The last level gives you five extra hearts and four points of armor, and your raised dead stay for good.",
    "",
    "A level 10 &5Lich&r with a &aGlass Bottle&r in the off-hand catches the soul of any villager, witch, illager or piglin it kills. Drinking a &6Soul in a Bottle&r heals a Lich two hearts.",
  ],
  "quest.17FAD6B414738DC2.quest_desc": [
    "A deck of cards that each place a lasting condition on you. Some are gifts and some are punishments, and a few are both.",
    "",
    "The wording on each card is exact about what it does. Read it before you draw, because most of them do not expire on their own.",
    "",
    "No recipe makes the deck. A &dFortune Teller&r villager sells it at master level for 24 &aEmeralds&r.",
    "",
    "A villager takes that job from a &2Crystal Ball&r, and the ball needs a &aSeer Stone&r from a night rite on &6Golden Ritual Chalk&r.",
  ],
  "quest.07C62222A3914CD9.title": "&dThe Spirit World",
  "quest.129860E2C9082F1C.quest_desc": [
    "The poppet that hurts the thing it is bound to, and it works on exactly what you would guess.",
    "",
    "Throw it in water to drown the target, into fire to burn them, off something tall to break them, or stab it with a needle.",
    "",
    "&cVoodoo Protection Poppet&r is the counter, and other people can craft one too.",
  ],
  "quest.5459984CD8A172E5.quest_desc": [
    "&cInfernal Rituals&r require very evil reagents. &3Refined Evil&r can be distilled in the ",
    "distillery. ",
    "",
    "Refer to the &bMod Guidebook&r for all the ritual placements. ",
  ],
  "quest.0E9C90976C66641C.title": "The Critter Snare",
  "quest.24ACDC2BB0A27070.quest_desc": [
    "A &dPhylactery&r holds a soul for you, and when you die it spends that soul to bring you back. It works from level 2 onward.",
    "",
    "The &bCreate Phylactery&r rite needs 10,000 &bAltar Power&r and a wide ring of &aBinding Chalk&r.",
    "",
    "Fill it with the &bBind Phylactery&r rite. Set the empty phylactery within four blocks of the circle's center, and the rite pulls the soul out of the nearest humanoid within 16 blocks.",
    "- &bGreater soul&r: villagers and piglins. You come back where you fell at half health.",
    "- &bLesser soul&r: illagers, zombie villagers and zombified piglins. You wake at the phylactery with a tenth of your health.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Level 9 needs the third tablet and one death that a phylactery saves.",
    "",
    "Keep every phylactery under open sky. From level 9, one that cannot see the sky gives you Slowness and Mining Fatigue.",
  ],
  "quest.74CB218EFCB2185A.quest_desc": [
    "Grow the &aBelladonna&r you planted and take its flower. That is the ingredient the &dGuidebook&r has been waiting on.",
    "",
    "It is the real documentation and it is large. Ten sections and over five hundred pages. This chapter walks the spine of it and points at the rest.",
    "",
    "&7&oKeep the book on you. JEI shows most recipes, but only the book explains how the machines and rituals behave.&r",
  ],
  "quest.44B05983766D847B.title": "&dPoppets",
  "quest.29656D8C06B7A2F7.quest_desc": [
    "The second long path. Wear the &aMoon Charm&r in a curio slot to take wolf or werewolf form, and take it off to change straight back.",
    "",
    "No recipe makes the &aMoon Charm&r. Place a &2Werewolf Altar&r, hand it three &aGold Ingots&r and take the charm off it with an empty hand a moment later.",
    "",
    "To advance a bloodline you build a Wicker Man out of &aBlood-Stained Hay&r and set it alight. The &cHorned Huntsman&r answers it, and you have to beat him.",
    "",
    "From the second bloodline the charm also gives you Blood Scent, which paints a path toward nearby living things until you dismiss it.",
  ],
  "quest.17FAD6B414738DC2.title": "&6The Tarot Deck",
  "quest.0D831CA92D518208.title": "&dMutandis Extremis",
  "task.4AE3B34BFEAE32D6.title": "Any Witches' Oven, iron or copper",
}